<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38198" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pransĭto</span></b> , āvi,
		1, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. freq.
				n.</i> and <i>a.</i> [prandeo]. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Neutr.</i>, <i>to breakfast</i>, <i>to eat breakfast</i> or <i>luncheon</i> (mostly ante- and postclass.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ad rivum accumbentes viatores pransitare
					solent,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr. 8,
					3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pransitans et cenitans,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lampr. Elag. 27</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>to breakfast upon</i>,
				<i>eat at breakfast</i> or <i>luncheon</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">polentam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. As. 1, 1, 20</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prolem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 4, 143</span></i>
			.—<i>Impers. pass.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ut pransitaretur et cenitaretur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 2, 13</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
